From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: apklayer <apklayer@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ClassInstrumentor: skip <init> calls of objects created before the super call

apklayer patch: extractCallToSuperConstructor took the first INVOKESPECIAL <init> whose owner is the class or its superclass as the
super()/this() call. A constructor that creates an object of its superclass as an argument of this(...) (AuthenticationRequiredException(Parcel):
this(new SecurityException(in.readString()), ...); IkeSessionStateMachine$IkeInitData) was cut inside the argument list: ASM's frame
computation then failed (NegativeArraySizeException: -2), PreInstrument left the class to the sandbox loader, and the sandbox loader threw
the same error at an app's first use of the class (DAVx5's Application.onCreate). <init> calls that initialise an object created by a
NEW in the constructor are now skipped.

Against external/robolectric 87aa52b08 (REVISION). Applied by runtime/meson.build onto the staged
upstream sources (<native>/aosp/robolectric-src); the result is compiled into native-runtime.jar ahead of Robolectric_all.jar.
---
diff --git a/sandbox/src/main/java/org/robolectric/internal/bytecode/ClassInstrumentor.java b/sandbox/src/main/java/org/robolectric/internal/bytecode/ClassInstrumentor.java
--- a/sandbox/src/main/java/org/robolectric/internal/bytecode/ClassInstrumentor.java
+++ b/sandbox/src/main/java/org/robolectric/internal/bytecode/ClassInstrumentor.java
@@ -485,14 +485,24 @@
     // Start removing instructions at the beginning of the method. The first instructions of
     // constructors may vary.
     int startIndex = 0;
+    // apklayer patch: objects the constructor creates before its super()/this() call (this(new SecurityException(..), ..)
+    // in AuthenticationRequiredException) are initialised by an <init> of the superclass too: that call is not the super call
+    int pendingNew = 0;
 
     AbstractInsnNode[] insns = ctor.instructions.toArray();
     for (int i = 0; i < insns.length; i++) {
       AbstractInsnNode node = insns[i];
 
       switch (node.getOpcode()) {
+        case Opcodes.NEW:
+          pendingNew++;
+          break;
         case Opcodes.INVOKESPECIAL:
           MethodInsnNode mnode = (MethodInsnNode) node;
+          if (pendingNew > 0 && "<init>".equals(mnode.name)) {
+            pendingNew--;
+            break;
+          }
           if (mnode.owner.equals(mutableClass.internalClassName)
               || mnode.owner.equals(mutableClass.classNode.superName)) {
             if (!"<init>".equals(mnode.name)) {
